-- title:
--   Switcheroo Complete Part Self Consistency Pair Bound
-- statement:
--   **Complete-part self consistency lifts to a slice-pair qSDD bound.**
--
--   Assume the family satisfies complete G self consistency at level `zeta`. Compare, for each slice-pair question, the left-tensor and right-tensor outcome operators of the indexed family. Their average qSDD core over the uniform slice-pair distribution is bounded by the same self-consistency error:
--
--   $$
--   \mathbb E_q\,\operatorname{qSDDCore}\left(\psi_{bi},
--   \operatorname{leftTensor}(F_{q.1,g}),
--   \operatorname{rightTensor}(F_{q.1,g})\right)\le\zeta.
--   $$
--
--   The result is the pair-distribution form used to control both fourth-term square-root transfers. It lifts a slicewise complete-part hypothesis without changing its error budget.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.switcherooCompletePartSelfConsistency_pairBound`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
